# Scene-level eval (MM-RAG-gje). Unlike smoke.jsonl and full.jsonl, every gold
# ref here carries a hand-verified `time_range`, so a hit only counts when it
# lands on the right MOMENT — not merely the right asset. Asset-level gold on a
# single-asset store scores 1.000 by construction and cannot detect a retrieval
# change; that is why the s0l fix and the graph question both had no instrument.
#
# Ranges were read off this asset's own transcript segments and OCR frames, then
# padded to the enclosing segment boundaries. Media is re-fetchable; nothing here
# is committed.
#
# Tags mark which stream *should* win, so `first-hit streams` in the report is a
# direct check on whether each stream earns its keep:
#   transcript — the answer is spoken
#   ocr        — the answer is ONLY on screen and never said aloud. These are the
#                discriminating cases: no transcript stream can reach them.
#   visual     — answerable from what is shown
